  ('c12-b4-t1', 'c12-bio-4', 'cbse-12-biology', '4.1', 'Mendel laws, incomplete dominance (Mirabilis jalapa), and codominance (ABO blood groups)', '', ARRAY['Mendel laws, incomplete dominance (Mirabilis jalapa), and codominance (ABO blood groups)']::TEXT[], NULL, true, true, 1),
  ('c12-b4-t2', 'c12-bio-4', 'cbse-12-biology', '4.2', 'Morgan Drosophila linkage experiments, recombination frequency, and sex determination in honey bees (haplodiploidy)', '', ARRAY['Morgan Drosophila linkage experiments, recombination frequency, and sex determination in honey bees (haplodiploidy)']::TEXT[], NULL, true, true, 2),
  ('c12-b4-t3', 'c12-bio-4', 'cbse-12-biology', '4.3', 'Pedigree analysis, Sickle-cell anaemia point mutation (GAG to GUG at beta-globin chain), and chromosomal aneuploidies (Down, Turner, Klinefelter)', '', ARRAY['Pedigree analysis, Sickle-cell anaemia point mutation (GAG to GUG at beta-globin chain), and chromosomal aneuploidies (Down, Turner, Klinefelter)']::TEXT[], NULL, true, true, 3),
  ('c12-bio-5-1', 'c12-bio-5', 'cbse-12-biology', '6.1', 'DNA Structure & Polynucleotide Chain', 'Chargaff''s rule applies strictly to DOUBLE-STRANDED DNA only. It does not apply to single-stranded RNA or single-stranded viral DNA.', ARRAY['Nucleotide components: Nitrogenous base (Purines A, G; Pyrimidines C, T, U), Pentose sugar, Phosphate group', 'Watson-Crick Double Helix: Anti-parallel strands (5''→3'' and 3''→5''), pitch = 3.4 nm (10 bp per turn, 0.34 nm between base pairs)', 'Chargaff''s Rule: A + G = C + T (A/T = 1 and G/C = 1 in dsDNA; ratio (A+T)/(G+C) is species-specific)', 'Histone octamer & Nucleosome: 200 bp wrapped around core of 8 basic histones (H2A, H2B, H3, H4) with H1 linker']::TEXT[], 'A + G = C + T, \quad \text{Pitch} = 3.4\text{ nm}, \quad \text{bp distance} = 0.34\text{ nm}', true, true, 1),
  ('c12-bio-5-2', 'c12-bio-5', 'cbse-12-biology', '6.2', 'Transforming Principle & Hershey-Chase Experiment', '³²P labels DNA (due to phosphate backbone); ³⁵S labels protein coat (due to sulfur-containing amino acids methionine and cysteine).', ARRAY['Griffith Experiment (1928): Heat-killed S-strain + Live R-strain injected into mice causes pneumonia and death (Transforming Principle)', 'Avery, MacLeod, McCarty (1944): DNase abolished transformation; proteases and RNase did not, proving DNA is the transforming substance', 'Hershey-Chase Experiment (1952): Used T2 bacteriophage labeled with ³⁵S (protein coat) and ³²P (DNA core). Only ³²P entered E. coli, providing unequivocal proof DNA is genetic material']::TEXT[], NULL, true, true, 2),
  ('c12-bio-5-3', 'c12-bio-5', 'cbse-12-biology', '6.3', 'DNA Replication & Meselson-Stahl Experiment', '', ARRAY['Semiconservative replication: Each daughter duplex contains one parental strand and one newly synthesized strand', 'Meselson-Stahl (1958): Used ¹⁵N heavy isotope and CsCl density gradient centrifugation in E. coli', 'After Gen 1 (20 min): 100% hybrid ¹⁴N-¹⁵N DNA; After Gen 2 (40 min): 50% hybrid, 50% light ¹⁴N-¹⁴N DNA', 'Taylor (1958) proved semiconservative replication in chromosomes using radioactive thymidine in Vicia faba', 'Enzymes: Helicase (unwinds), DNA Polymerase (synthesizes 5''→3'', needs RNA primer), Okazaki fragments on lagging strand joined by DNA Ligase']::TEXT[], '\text{Polymerization Direction: } 5'' \to 3''', true, true, 3),
  ('c12-bio-5-4', 'c12-bio-5', 'cbse-12-biology', '6.4', 'Transcription & Genetic Code', 'The coding strand DOES NOT actually participate in transcription, but mRNA sequence matches coding strand (with U replacing T).', ARRAY['Transcription unit: Promoter, Structural gene, Terminator; Template strand (3''→5'') vs Coding strand (5''→3'')', 'Genetic Code features: Triplet (61 codons for 20 amino acids, 3 stop codons: UAA, UAG, UGA), Degenerate, Unambiguous, Universal, Commaless; AUG codes for Methionine and is Start codon', 'Post-transcriptional processing in eukaryotes: Capping (7-methylguanosine triphosphate at 5'' end), Tailing (Poly-A tail at 3'' end), Splicing (Introns removed by spliceosome)']::TEXT[], NULL, true, true, 4),
  ('c12-bio-5-5', 'c12-bio-5', 'cbse-12-biology', '6.5', 'Translation & Regulation (Lac Operon)', 'Glucose is preferred over lactose; if glucose is present, the lac operon remains repressed even if lactose is available (catabolite repression).', ARRAY['Translation: Activation of amino acids (aminoacyl-tRNA synthetase), Initiation, Elongation (Peptidyl transferase ribozyme 28S rRNA), Termination', 'Lac Operon (Jacob & Monod): Polycistronic structural genes z (β-galactosidase), y (permease), a (transacetylase)', 'Inducer: Lactose (or allolactose) binds repressor protein, inactivating it and switching operon ON', 'Negative regulation: Lac repressor is synthesized constitutively by i-gene and binds operator o in absence of lactose']::TEXT[], NULL, true, true, 5),
  ('c12-b6-t1', 'c12-bio-6', 'cbse-12-biology', '6.1', 'Miller-Urey experiment, homologous vs analogous organs, and industrial melanism natural selection', '', ARRAY['Miller-Urey experiment, homologous vs analogous organs, and industrial melanism natural selection']::TEXT[], NULL, true, true, 1),
